      "type": "sceneBreak"
    },
    {
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Atop the mast, Juana lifts the hems of her dress, as if stepping atop the setting sun.\nThe fading light adorns her dress with a golden glow.\nWind lifts white grains of salt from the ground like blowing snow.\nAll eyes are fixated upon her dance, both on this ship and the other."
    },
    {
      "type": "sceneBreak"
    },
    {
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "They look up in silence. The ships sail in opposite directions, with only a few eyes glancing at the sea of white salt before them, and the sunset growing closer or further.\nAway they go, until the figures on the other ship have become as small as grains of salt."
    },
